{"lemma":"חָצַב","translit":"châtsab","pronunciation":"khaw-tsab'","def":"to cut or carve (wood, stone or other material); by implication, to hew, split, square, quarry, engrave","kjv":"cut, dig, divide, grave, hew (out, -er), made, mason.","occ":[[27,6,5,"Therefore have I hewed"],[22,22,16,"What hast thou here? and whom hast thou here, that thou hast hewed thee out"],[17,19,24,"That they were graven"],[11,12,12,"and hewers"],[12,22,15,"hewers"],[14,3,7,"also unto the masons"],[22,10,15,"itself against him that heweth"],[18,29,7,"divideth"],[13,26,10,"and digged"],[22,22,16,"he that heweth him out"],[19,9,1,"she hath hewn out"],[4,6,11,"digged"],[13,2,18,"hewers"],[4,6,11,"which thou diggedst"],[12,22,2,"masons"],[10,5,15,"hewers"],[22,5,2,"of it, and also made"],[22,51,1,"ye are hewn"],[12,22,2,"to hew"],[13,2,2,"to hew"],[23,2,13,"hewed them out"],[13,24,12,"masons"],[15,9,25,"digged"],[4,8,9,"thou mayest dig"],[22,51,9,"thou not it that hath cut"]]}